from (values
('127.698.d.6.B',3,'Re-projecting a downloaded image means:','["deleting it", "renaming only", "changing it to match the map''s coordinate system", "printing it twice"]'::jsonb,2,'Layers must share a projection.','original'),
('127.698.d.6.B',4,'If two layers appear in different places even though they cover the same area, the likely cause is:','["a loose cable", "a dirty screen", "a low battery", "mismatched projections or coordinate systems"]'::jsonb,3,'Projection mismatch shifts layers.','original'),
('127.698.d.6.C',3,'A device in an aircraft that detects reflected energy from the ground is:','["remote sensing equipment", "a cookbook", "a printer", "a clock"]'::jsonb,0,'Sensors on platforms collect imagery.','original'),
('127.698.d.6.C',4,'GPS differs from remote sensing because GPS:','["measures soil moisture only", "determines a position from satellite signals", "records weather only", "captures images from far away"]'::jsonb,1,'GPS locates positions; remote sensing images.','original'),
('127.698.d.6.D',3,'A handheld GPS device measures:','["only sound", "only time zones", "position, distance and elevation", "only temperature"]'::jsonb,2,'Handhelds provide basic measurements.','original'),
('127.698.d.6.D',4,'To measure the length of a trail with a handheld GPS, a technician:','["skips recording", "draws it from memory", "guesses the distance", "records a track while walking the trail"]'::jsonb,3,'Tracks record paths.','original'),
('127.698.d.6.E',3,'A drone differs from a satellite because a drone:','["can be flown at low altitude for fine detail on demand", "needs no pilot rules", "cannot carry sensors", "orbits the Earth forever"]'::jsonb,0,'Drones give flexible, high-resolution coverage.','original'),
('127.698.d.6.E',4,'A limitation of unmanned aerial sensing is:','["no sensors", "weather, battery life and flight rules limiting coverage", "unlimited flight time", "worldwide coverage at once"]'::jsonb,1,'Drones have operating limits.','original'),
('127.698.d.7.A',3,'A GIS investigation starts with:','["choosing a font", "printing the map", "asking a question and forming a hypothesis", "closing the file"]'::jsonb,2,'Investigations begin with questions.','original'),
('127.698.d.7.A',4,'A well-planned GIS investigation includes:','["only a title", "a random guess", "no steps", "the question, needed data, methods and a schedule"]'::jsonb,3,'Plans guide efficient work.','original'),
('127.698.d.7.B',3,'A student collects GIS data by recording locations of storm drains with GPS. This is:','["data collection", "map framing", "report printing", "data deletion"]'::jsonb,0,'Fieldwork gathers spatial data.','original'),
('127.698.d.7.B',4,'Good GIS data collection requires that each record has:','["no description", "accurate location and clear attribute information", "a random name", "a missing location"]'::jsonb,1,'Complete records are usable.','original'),
('127.698.d.7.C',3,'After collecting data, the analyst organizes it, analyzes it and:','["throws it away", "renames it as unknown", "draws conclusions and may predict trends", "hides it"]'::jsonb,2,'Analysis leads to inferences.','original'),
('127.698.d.7.C',4,'Spotting that crime reports increase each summer and forecasting next year''s pattern is:','["a file backup", "a printing error", "a projection change", "predicting a trend from GIS data"]'::jsonb,3,'Trends support predictions.','original'),
('127.698.d.7.D',3,'When reporting results, an analyst should use:','["correct GIS vocabulary and supporting maps", "random terms", "no evidence", "slang only"]'::jsonb,0,'Clear communication needs vocabulary and visuals.','original'),
('127.698.d.7.D',4,'A valid conclusion in a GIS report is one that:','["ignores the data", "is supported by the data and maps shown", "contradicts the maps", "is only an opinion"]'::jsonb,1,'Conclusions follow evidence.','original'),
('127.698.d.8.A',3,'To evaluate a local flooding problem, a team first identifies:','["the file size", "the weather forecast only", "the problem and the data needed", "the colors of the map"]'::jsonb,2,'Define the problem, then gather data.','original'),
('127.698.d.8.A',4,'For a local erosion project, necessary data might include:','["recipes", "music files", "sports scores", "elevation, soil and land cover layers"]'::jsonb,3,'Relevant layers support analysis.','original'),
('127.698.d.8.B',3,'A project plan for a GIS study should include:','["tasks and a schedule for completing them", "no dates", "random steps", "only a title"]'::jsonb,0,'Plans need tasks and timeline.','original'),
('127.698.d.8.B',4,'A schedule helps a GIS team by:','["hiding the steps", "showing what must be done and when", "removing deadlines", "skipping tasks"]'::jsonb,1,'Schedules keep work on track.','original'),
('127.698.d.8.C',3,'A team uses satellite images to create a map of the problem area. This is:','["printing a blank sheet", "writing a recipe", "creating a GIS map from remote sensing images", "deleting layers"]'::jsonb,2,'Imagery supports maps.','original'),
('127.698.d.8.C',4,'When creating a problem map, the team should include:','["no labels", "only a photo", "only a border", "a title, legend, scale and north arrow"]'::jsonb,3,'Map elements aid interpretation.','original'),
('127.698.d.8.D',3,'Looking at map features to find which areas are most at risk is:','["evaluating map features to identify solutions", "changing fonts", "deleting layers", "renaming layers"]'::jsonb,0,'Evaluation points to solutions.','original'),
('127.698.d.8.D',4,'If a map shows runoff collecting in one low area, a likely solution to evaluate is:','["removing the map", "adding drainage or retention there", "ignoring the area", "building in the low area"]'::jsonb,1,'Evidence guides solutions.','original'),
('127.698.d.8.E',3,'Using raster GIS to model how water flows over terrain helps to:','["create passwords", "print posters", "develop solutions to reduce flooding", "edit audio"]'::jsonb,2,'Models support solution design.','original'),
('127.698.d.8.E',4,'A raster analysis that finds the steepest paths of runoff supports solving problems by:','["deleting the data", "hiding the map", "changing the title", "showing where to place controls"]'::jsonb,3,'Analysis locates intervention points.','original'),
('127.698.d.8.F',3,'At the end of a project, findings are shared in a:','["final report or poster", "hidden file", "random note", "blank page"]'::jsonb,0,'Reports communicate results.','original'),
('127.698.d.8.F',4,'A final report on a local problem should present:','["only the cover", "the data, analysis, maps and recommended solution", "only jokes", "only a single number"]'::jsonb,1,'Reports tell the complete story.','original'),
('127.699.d.1.A',3,'A student who enjoys drones and maps might consider a career as a:','["court reporter", "florist", "remote sensing technician", "pastry chef"]'::jsonb,2,'Remote sensing careers use sensors and imagery.','original'),
('127.699.d.1.A',4,'Which employer commonly hires people trained in spatial technology and remote sensing?','["a movie theater", "a hair salon", "a toy store", "a utility company monitoring its power lines"]'::jsonb,3,'Utilities map and inspect infrastructure.','original'),
('127.699.d.1.B',3,'A student sits in with a surveyor for a day to see the job. This is:','["job shadowing", "a final test", "a license", "a loan"]'::jsonb,0,'Shadowing exposes students to real work.','original'),
('127.699.d.1.B',4,'Another career preparation experience is:','["a video game", "an internship at an engineering firm", "a long vacation", "a lunch break"]'::jsonb,1,'Internships provide practice.','original'),
('127.699.d.1.C',3,'Certifications help a spatial technology worker by:','["ending the career", "replacing all training", "proving their skills to employers", "closing a file"]'::jsonb,2,'Certifications signal competence.','original'),
('127.699.d.1.C',4,'Which would be an industry certification for a drone operator?','["a swim badge", "a library card", "a gym pass", "a Part 107 remote pilot certificate"]'::jsonb,3,'Commercial drone work requires an FAA certificate.','original'),
('127.699.d.1.D',3,'Flying a drone over a private backyard and recording it raises a concern about:','["privacy", "gravity", "paper", "batteries"]'::jsonb,0,'Imagery can invade privacy.','original'),
('127.699.d.1.D',4,'An ethical remote sensing professional should:','["ignore all rules", "follow laws and respect people''s privacy", "sell private images", "record anyone"]'::jsonb,1,'Ethics and legality guide the work.','original'),
('127.699.d.2.A',3,'The Mercator projection keeps the correct:','["size of all countries", "temperature of oceans", "shape and direction of small areas, stretching land near the poles", "speed of ships"]'::jsonb,2,'Mercator preserves direction but distorts area at high latitudes.','original'),
('127.699.d.2.A',4,'On a Mercator map, Greenland appears much larger than it really is because:','["Greenland has grown", "the scale is 1:1", "maps are wrong by law", "the projection stretches areas near the poles"]'::jsonb,3,'Area distortion increases with latitude.','original'),
('127.699.d.2.B',3,'The Albers conic projection is often used for maps of:','["mid-latitude regions like the continental United States", "a single room", "the Moon", "the North Pole only"]'::jsonb,0,'Albers suits east-west mid-latitude areas.','original'),
('127.699.d.2.B',4,'The Albers conic projection is useful for statistics maps because it:','["preserves all directions", "preserves area", "has no distortion", "shows no borders"]'::jsonb,1,'Equal-area projections suit comparisons.','original'),
('127.699.d.2.C',3,'Different map projections were developed because:','["maps are free", "ink is cheap", "no flat map can show the curved Earth without some distortion", "the Earth is flat"]'::jsonb,2,'Every projection compromises.','original'),
('127.699.d.2.C',4,'A mapmaker picks a projection to match the map''s:','["paper color", "printer", "title length", "purpose, such as navigation or area comparison"]'::jsonb,3,'Purpose guides projection choice.','original'),
('127.699.d.3.A',3,'In GPS terms, a waypoint is:','["a saved location with coordinates", "a battery", "a map border", "a satellite''s name"]'::jsonb,0,'Waypoints are stored positions.','original'),
('127.699.d.3.A',4,'A recorded line of positions showing the path you traveled is a:','["scale", "track", "title", "legend"]'::jsonb,1,'Tracks record movement.','original'),
('127.699.d.3.B',3,'A GPS receiver gets its position by using signals from:','["radio towers only", "wall clocks", "satellites", "street signs"]'::jsonb,2,'GPS uses satellite signals.','original'),
('127.699.d.3.B',4,'The antenna of a GPS receiver should be:','["wrapped in foil", "buried underground", "placed inside a drawer", "oriented with a clear view of the sky"]'::jsonb,3,'Open sky improves reception.','original'),
('127.699.d.3.C',3,'Mapping fire hydrant locations with GPS helps a city to:','["find and maintain them for emergencies", "paint murals", "bake bread", "write songs"]'::jsonb,0,'Asset mapping aids public safety.','original'),
('127.699.d.3.C',4,'Utility crews use GPS coordinates to:','["create playlists", "locate buried pipes and poles", "design logos", "write novels"]'::jsonb,1,'Coordinates guide field work.','original'),
('127.699.d.3.D',3,'A smartphone''s built-in GPS is usually:','["more accurate than any receiver", "unable to find locations", "less accurate than a survey-grade receiver", "free of satellites"]'::jsonb,2,'Consumer devices have larger errors.','original'),
('127.699.d.3.D',4,'A surveyor needs centimeter-level accuracy, so they use:','["a paper map", "a hand-drawn sketch", "a phone with no signal", "a high-precision survey-grade GPS receiver"]'::jsonb,3,'Specialized receivers give higher accuracy.','original'),
('127.699.d.4.A',3,'A satellite is a type of:','["aerial or space remote sensing platform", "chair", "kitchen appliance", "underwater platform"]'::jsonb,0,'Satellites carry sensors from orbit.','original'),
('127.699.d.4.A',4,'An underwater vehicle that maps the seafloor is a:','["weather balloon", "submersible remote sensing platform", "airplane", "satellite"]'::jsonb,1,'Submersibles operate underwater.','original'),
('127.699.d.4.B',3,'To map a small construction site often, the best platform is probably:','["a deep space probe", "a submarine", "a drone", "a weather satellite"]'::jsonb,2,'Drones give frequent, detailed coverage.','original'),
('127.699.d.4.B',4,'The best platform for mapping an entire continent''s vegetation is:','["a handheld camera", "a kite", "a backyard drone", "a satellite"]'::jsonb,3,'Satellites cover large areas.','original'),
('127.699.d.4.C',3,'A camera sensor on a drone captures:','["visible-light photographs", "soil by touch", "smells", "radio music"]'::jsonb,0,'Cameras record visible light.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
