('127.699.d.6.B',3,'A map shaded only to display average rainfall across a state is an example of a thematic map, which focuses on:','["only a legend", "no data", "one topic such as population density across an area", "every topic at once"]'::jsonb,2,'Thematic maps focus on a theme.','original'),
('127.699.d.6.B',4,'Planning a thematic map includes choosing the theme, the data classes and:','["a blank page", "a random font", "no title", "the colors and legend"]'::jsonb,3,'Design decisions follow the theme.','original'),
('127.699.d.6.C',3,'Turning a flat map into a 3D view with building heights helps to:','["show feature heights and terrain visually", "print less", "hide the data", "delete layers"]'::jsonb,0,'3D shows vertical dimension.','original'),
('127.699.d.6.C',4,'A 3D map of a city can demonstrate:','["a battery''s size", "how tall buildings are relative to each other", "the printer''s age", "the user''s name"]'::jsonb,1,'Height data becomes visible in 3D.','original'),
('127.699.d.6.D',3,'After mapping income by area, a student draws a conclusion and:','["makes it up", "hides the map", "justifies it with the map and data", "ignores the data"]'::jsonb,2,'Conclusions need support.','original'),
